{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>On Mount Sinai.</b> What has the sabbatical year to do with Mount Sinai? Were not all the commandments stated from Sinai? Rather: just as the sabbatical year — its general principles, its specific details, and its precise rules were stated from Sinai, so too all of them — their general principles and their precise rules were stated from Sinai. Thus it is taught in Torat Kohanim; and it seems to me that this is its meaning: since we do not find the sabbatical year of lands repeated in the plains of Moab in Mishneh Torah, we learn that its general principles and its specific details — all of them — were stated from Sinai. And the verse comes and teaches here about every utterance that was spoken to Moses, that from Sinai they all were — their general principles and their precise rules — and they were repeated again in the plains of Moab."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:11.426068229Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}